# DAW Timeline Rules

## Component Hierarchy

```
DAWTimeline.tsx              ← main container: ruler, export buttons, global playback controls
  └─ DAWGroup.tsx            ← groups sounds by usage parent
       └─ DAWTrack.tsx       ← one track per sound; mute/solo state; drag-to-reorder iterations
            └─ DAWIteration.tsx  ← one WaveSurfer instance per audio iteration
```

All files: `frontend/src/components/audio/daw/`

## WaveSurfer — One Instance Per Iteration

**Never share a WaveSurfer instance between iterations or tracks.**
Each `DAWIteration` creates and owns its own instance:

```typescript
// DAWIteration.tsx — standard lifecycle
const wsRef = useRef<WaveSurfer | null>(null)

useEffect(() => {
  wsRef.current = WaveSurfer.create({
    container: containerRef.current,
    ...WAVESURFER_TIMELINE,            // constants from utils/constants.ts
  })
  wsRef.current.load(audioUrl)
  return () => {
    wsRef.current?.destroy()
    wsRef.current = null
  }
}, [audioUrl])
```

WaveSurfer config constants: `frontend/src/utils/constants.ts` → `WAVESURFER_TIMELINE`

## Timeline Playback Sync

`useTimelinePlayback` is the single source of playback time:

- Returns `{ isPlaying, currentTime, duration, play, pause, stop, seek }`
- Uses a `requestAnimationFrame` loop while playing — updates `currentTime` at ≈60fps
- Each `DAWIteration` reads `currentTime` and calls `ws.seekTo(currentTime / duration)`

**Do not** create secondary `requestAnimationFrame` loops inside individual track or iteration
components. All time updates must flow from `useTimelinePlayback`.

## audioControlsStore — Playback Control State

Single source of truth for all runtime playback state.
Import from `@/store` barrel: `const { soundVolumes, mutedSounds } = useAudioControlsStore()`

| Field | Type | Purpose |
| ----- | ---- | ------- |
| `soundVolumes` | `Record<soundId, number>` | Per-sound volume 0–1 |
| `selectedVariants` | `Record<soundId, variantId>` | Active audio variant per sound |
| `soundIntervals` | `Record<soundId, IntervalConfig>` | Loop interval / start offset per sound |
| `mutedSounds` | `Set<soundId>` | Muted sound IDs |
| `soloedSound` | `soundId \| null` | Exclusively audible sound (`null` = none) |
| `timelineDurationMs` | `number` | Total timeline length in milliseconds |

## Export Formats

`frontend/src/lib/audio/SoundscapeExporter.ts` handles all export formats:

| Format | Channels | Use for |
| ------ | -------- | ------- |
| Mono | 1 | Basic reference / checking mix |
| Binaural | 2 | Headphone listening |
| FOA | 4 | 1st-order ambisonics (VR, spatial audio) |
| TOA | 16 | 3rd-order ambisonics (high-quality spatial) |

Exporter accepts an optional limiter flag to prevent clipping on multi-sound mixdowns.

## Adding New DAW Features

| Feature type | Where to edit |
| ------------ | ------------- |
| Per-track UI (e.g. record button) | `DAWTrack.tsx` |
| Per-iteration visual (e.g. waveform colour) | `DAWIteration.tsx` |
| Global control (e.g. master tempo) | `DAWTimeline.tsx` + new field in `audioControlsStore` |
| New export format | `SoundscapeExporter.ts` + expose option in `DAWTimeline.tsx` |
| Playback behaviour change | `useTimelinePlayback.ts` only — do not split logic across components |
